    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C214", "C234", "C226", "C253", "C238", "C252", "C246"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No drospirenone-specific absolute oral bioavailability, hepatic clearance, or metabolic-stability record is present in any level.",
    "L6 hepatic-clearance records are for other steroids/compounds; the closest spirolactone records (canrenone C214, eplerenone C234/C226/C253) do not provide a quantitative F or first-pass extraction value.",
    "L6 records are in vitro/in situ/in silico and do not measure oral F; no IV-oral comparison for drospirenone is available.",
    "No drospirenone-specific solubility or dissolution measurement is available; the unfavorable solubility prior is not affirmative evidence of F<20%.",
    "Query species, formulation, dose, prandial state, and disease condition are unspecified; species-dependent F remains possible.",
    "L3 oral AUC records lack IV comparators and measure canrenone or co-administered hormones, not drospirenone itself."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 hepatic-clearance records are mostly for structurally distant steroids and do not provide drospirenone-specific F or first-pass loss; the closest spirolactone records (canrenone moderate esterase CLint, eplerenone CYP3A4 substrate without quantitative F) do not affirmatively support F<20%. Combined with L4/L5 high absorption/permeability evidence for lipophilic steroids and L3 canrenone oral exposure, F>=20% remains better supported. Prediction high, moderate confidence, keep."
}

